  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnerships for Growth: Women Entrepreneurs Finance (We-Fi) Initiative - Scaling the Care Economy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Women Entrepreneurs Finance Initiative (We-Fi) Care Call is a global initiative to empower women entrepreneurs to scale innovative solutions in the care economy, addressing critical gaps in affordable, quality care while driving inclusive growth. By providing blended finance, technical assistance, and market access through multilateral development bank partners, the Care Call aims to reduce unpaid care burdens, increase women&#x2019;s economic participation, and create decent jobs, unlocking opportunities across childcare, eldercare, health, and digital care services. This effort not only strengthens care systems but also accelerates gender equality and economic resilience in developing countries. This partnership forms part of the Jobs and Inclusive Growth Centre of Expertise which will also leverage the knowledge and expert advice of the initiative to inform other components of the COE.</narrative>
  </description>
